new_rwcas=the constructor: allocates a fresh cell
read=the read operation (a plain dereference)
write=the write operation: CmpXchg against the value just read, with a prophecy
value=the abstract state of the cell -- what a client owns and reasons about
rwcas_inv=the main invariant, protecting the physical cell and the request registry
write_inv=the per-writer invariant holding a pending atomic update, for helping
registry_inv=ties each registered request to its linearization flag
registry=authoritative ownership of the request registry
registered=fragmental ownership of a single request
AU_write=the atomic update a writer holds
AU_read=the atomic update a reader holds
is_rwcas=the client-facing "this value is a cell" predicate
extract_result=reads the prophecy: did the CmpXchg succeed, and with what value
rwcasN=the namespace of the main invariant
writeN=the namespace of the per-writer invariants
linearize_writes=linearizes all pending writers while preserving the registry invariant
registry_update=allocates a new request in the registry
registry_agree=the authoritative registry agrees with a fragment
